<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose seven points to 1,361.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose seven points to 1,361.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,361 today from 1,354 on July 8, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p>  Route Index     Rate    Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1437    13.050	  1429    12.969</p>
<p>   1a   1342 10163.000	  1334 10106.000</p>
<p>   2    1708    24.406	  1687    24.094</p>
<p>   2a   1615 13244.000	  1591 13044.000</p>
<p>   3    1481    13.663	  1476    13.619</p>
<p>   3a   1272 10038.000	  1267 10000.000</p>
<p>   6    1286    13.269	  1287    13.275</p>
<p>   7    1194     5.813	  1195     5.819</p>
<p>   8     851     9.356	   850     9.344</p>
<p>   9     798  6981.000	   800  6994.000</p>
<p>  10    1158     5.850	  1159     5.856</p>
